course: dictionary
lesson: 1547
title: Challenger: the one who tries to win
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A challenger is someone who wants to take the top place from the person who has it now. In a game, the champion holds the title, and the challenger tries to beat them.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The challenger to the champion played hard in every round.» The words champion and round tell you who is trying to win the title.
explain: The word can also mean someone who questions whether something is right or true. A challenger in a debate asks, "Is that really true?" Read the context to see which meaning fits.
explain: Watch for capital letters. «The Challenger Deep in the Mariana Trench is the deepest point of the ocean» uses Challenger as a name for a place, not as a person. A name is a special label, so it is not the word's meaning.
fact: A challenger is a person or team that tries to beat the champion or winner.
fact: «A new challenger» means someone fresh who wants to take the top place.
fact: A challenger can also be a person who questions whether something is right or true.
fact: Challenger Deep is a name for a very deep place in the Pacific Ocean, so it has a capital letter.
fact: «The deepest known point of the ocean is the Challenger Deep in the Mariana Trench, about 10,900 metres down.» Here the name shows where the place is, not who is trying to win.
exercise: «The challenger to the champion trained every day for the final.» Who is the challenger? | *The one trying to beat the champion | The crowd | The champion who already holds the title | The referee
exercise: Mia stood up in the meeting and asked, «Is this plan really fair?» What role is Mia playing? | The champion, who already holds the title | A spectator | *A challenger, who questions whether something is right
exercise: «The Challenger Deep is the deepest point of the ocean.» Why does Challenger have a capital letter here? | It is a person's name | It means the winner | It starts a new sentence only | *It is the name of a place
test: «The new challenger scored two goals in the first half.» In a sports match, what does new challenger mean? | The referee | Someone who has already won the cup | A fan who is watching from the stands | *Someone trying to beat the champion
test: «The strong challenger for the seat asked hard questions about the plan.» What is the challenger trying to do in this election? | Hand the seat to the champion | Sell the seat to a museum | *Win the seat | Stop the election
exam: What does challenger mean in «The challenger to the champion has never lost a game»? | A place where games are played | *Someone trying to beat the champion | The champion's coach | A prize for winning
